name duel-merge-1
timeout 300

# THE ASYMMETRIC DUEL, GEOMETRY 6: THE MERGE — the one place the MiG-29's weapon set is not the
# inferior one, and therefore the mission that has to exist before the campaign may claim the F-16
# dominates. The four BVR geometries all turn on radar reach and Rtr, and on both the MiG is behind by
# construction (2.0x and 1.7x, measured). Inside the merge neither matters: an R-73 is cued off the
# helmet, a GSh-301 round carries 2.7x the energy of an M61A1 round, and the airframe out-turns and
# out-rolls the F-16 (measured corner 420 kt / 24.2 deg/s against 380 / 16.2; roll plant 201 deg/s per
# full deflection against 78.7).
#
# THE SETUP: 8 km apart, head-on, co-altitude, both on `set task bfm` — the close-combat control law
# on both sides, no BVR phase and no long shot. Both start inside every launch zone either side has.
#
# THE MiG's RADAR IS IN RAD, NOT IN A CLOSE-COMBAT MODE, and that is this aircraft's own constraint
# rather than a setting: the N019's ACM patterns are PENCILS in azimuth (+-1.75 deg CC, +-1.5 VS,
# +-1.25 BORE, sensors.md §4.9), so a manoeuvring fighter cannot acquire with them. RAD is +-30 deg
# and finds him, but it does not auto-lock, so the pilot has to designate with his thumb over the
# command bus (pilot/FBPilot::BfmDesignate). The F-16 is in ACM HUD, which auto-locks.
#
# READING RULE: exit 2, `fulcrum result=LOC`, and it is a REPRODUCER FOR A KNOWN GAP rather than a
# duel — the same role missions/test-gear-up-crash.fbm plays for the flight monitor. The MiG cannot
# fight a merge today and this file is the shortest statement of why.
# MEASURED: the F-16's ACM HUD pattern auto-locks at t=1.9 (3.81 nm). The MiG gets ZERO radar contacts
# in the whole run, and 22.8 s after the merge starts its close-combat law has rolled it through
# -150 deg of bank at 29 deg of incidence and the flight monitor calls a stall/mush departure
# (t=24.7 s, roll 91.9 deg, p=-94.8 deg/s, vs=-30.2 m/s). Two separate causes, both open in
# modules/mig29/module.md: gap 4h (the ACM patterns are pencils in azimuth, the cold-search law rolls
# the jet before its first two looks land) and the departure itself, which gap 4h did not yet name.
# Until both are closed, "the MiG-29 wins the merge" is an untested claim and doc/duels.md says so.

unit viper
  team friendly
  module f16
  spawn 46.90000 6.95000 5000 90.0 380
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode acm_hud                      # auto-locks the nearest firm track: no thumb needed
  set fcr_range_nm 10
  set rwr on
  set store 3 aim9
  set store 7 aim9
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task bfm
  wp 46.90000 7.20000 5000 380
  objective kill unit fulcrum
  objective survive

unit fulcrum
  team hostile
  module mig29
  spawn 46.90000 7.05500 5000 270.0 380
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set n019_mode rad                         # the only pattern wide enough to find a manoeuvring jet
  set n019_range_nm 10
  set n019_emission illum
  set rwr on
  set store 3 r73
  set store 4 r73
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task bfm
  wp 46.90000 6.80000 5000 380
  objective kill unit viper
  objective survive
